{
  "_comment": [
    "First-boot setup: the engine and the surface that draws it.",
    "",
    "Two services rather than one, on the same split installerd and install-tui",
    "use. oobed creates the account and names the machine, which needs SYSTEM;",
    "oobe-tui draws boxes on a terminal, which needs nothing. Merging them",
    "would put a TUI in a SYSTEM process for the sake of one fewer key.",
    "",
    "THIS SEED IS FOR AN INSTALLED MACHINE, NOT A BOOT MEDIUM. The edition",
    "lists it in `install_autoapply`, so peiso stages it into",
    "lcl/policy/autoapply.install.d/ -- which peinit does not drain -- and the",
    "installer promotes it into the target's autoapply.d/. A live image that",
    "applied it would find setup taking the console away from the installer.",
    "",
    "It runs exactly once. On success oobed removes both of these keys and",
    "exits, so the second boot has no setup to do and no definitions left to",
    "explain. On failure it removes nothing: retiring would delete the only",
    "route back to the question, and a machine with no account yet cannot be",
    "logged into to put it back by hand. So a failed setup is recovered by",
    "rebooting into the same flow.",
    "",
    "== oobed ==",
    "",
    "Readiness is Notify (0), unlike installerd's Alive. oobe-tui `Requires`",
    "this service, and with Alive readiness 'started' means the process exists",
    "-- which says nothing about whether the socket has been bound. The surface",
    "would connect to nothing, exit, and take the console with it, and the",
    "login prompt would come up on a machine with no accounts. oobed sends",
    "READY=1 after bind, so the ordering is real.",
    "",
    "RestartPolicy is Never (0) because oobed exits deliberately when setup is",
    "done. Restarting it would relaunch a daemon whose definition it has just",
    "deleted.",
    "",
    "Trigger is plain `boot`: the engine has no terminal and no reason to wait",
    "for a quiet one.",
    "",
    "== oobe-tui ==",
    "",
    "TTYPath is /dev/console with TTYPrecedence 100. login-console names the",
    "same device at the default precedence of 0, so on this boot peinit gives",
    "the console here and skips the login prompt (TtyUnavailable) rather than",
    "letting the two interleave. When oobe-tui exits, login-console's",
    "`tty:released` trigger brings the prompt up. 100 rather than 1 to leave",
    "room: this is not the only thing that will ever want a console ahead of a",
    "login prompt, and a recovery shell should be able to outrank it.",
    "",
    "boot:settled for the same reason login-console uses it: peinit writes its",
    "progress to /dev/console, and a form started mid-boot is drawn over.",
    "",
    "RestartPolicy is OnFailure (1) with the default budget. A transient crash",
    "gets another go; a persistent one gives up, which releases the console and",
    "produces a login prompt. That prompt is on a machine with no accounts and",
    "so is not much use -- but the alternative is a terminal held forever by a",
    "service that cannot draw on it, and at least this way the failure is",
    "visible and the recovery is the install medium.",
    "",
    "Requires lpsd, not authd: authd being up means an account could be",
    "authenticated, lpsd being up means one can be created. Same reasoning as",
    "login-console, and lpsd requires authd, so this orders after both.",
    "",
    "TERM=vt220 to match login-console: a serial console is the common case for",
    "this image.",
    "",
    "Identity is SYSTEM, which for a program drawing boxes on a terminal wants",
    "justifying. oobed's socket is reachable by SYSTEM and Administrators, and",
    "on a machine that has not been set up there are no administrators yet --",
    "that is the situation this exists to end. A surface that could not connect",
    "would exit and hand the console to a login prompt with nothing to log in",
    "as. install-tui runs as the operator precisely because by then there is",
    "one.",
    "",
    "Shipped by dev.peios.oobe into /usr/share/regim/; inert until an image",
    "names it in [registry] install_autoapply."
  ],
  "keys": [
    { "path": "Machine\\System" },
    { "path": "Machine\\System\\Services" },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Services\\oobed",
      "values": [
        { "name": "ImagePath",     "type": "sz",    "data": "/sbin/oobed" },
        { "name": "Triggers",      "type": "multi", "data": ["boot"] },
        { "name": "Requires",      "type": "multi", "data": ["lpsd"] },
        { "name": "Identity",      "type": "sz",    "data": "SYSTEM" },
        { "name": "Readiness",     "type": "dword", "data": 0 },
        { "name": "RestartPolicy", "type": "dword", "data": 0 },
        { "name": "ErrorControl",  "type": "dword", "data": 0 },
        { "name": "DisplayName",   "type": "sz",    "data": "First-boot setup" },
        { "name": "Description",   "type": "sz",    "data": "Creates the first account and names the machine, over MSIP" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Services\\oobe-tui",
      "values": [
        { "name": "ImagePath",      "type": "sz",    "data": "/bin/oobe-tui" },
        { "name": "TTYPath",        "type": "sz",    "data": "/dev/console" },
        { "name": "TTYPrecedence",  "type": "dword", "data": 100 },
        { "name": "Triggers",       "type": "multi", "data": ["boot:settled"] },
        { "name": "Requires",       "type": "multi", "data": ["oobed"] },
        { "name": "Identity",       "type": "sz",    "data": "SYSTEM" },
        { "name": "Readiness",      "type": "dword", "data": 1 },
        { "name": "RestartPolicy",  "type": "dword", "data": 1 },
        { "name": "ErrorControl",   "type": "dword", "data": 0 },
        { "name": "Environment",    "type": "multi", "data": ["TERM=vt220"] },
        { "name": "DisplayName",    "type": "sz",    "data": "First-boot setup (console)" },
        { "name": "Description",    "type": "sz",    "data": "Terminal surface for first-boot setup, on the system console" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
